=== HINT 1 ===
In C23, bool/true/false are keywords - use them directly.
If compilation fails, make sure your compiler is invoked with -std=c2x or -std=c23.

=== HINT 2 ===
Palindrome check:
  int len = (int)strlen(s);
  for (int i = 0; i < len / 2; i++) {
      if (s[i] != s[len - 1 - i]) return false;
  }
  return true;

=== HINT 3 (SPOILER) ===
bool is_palindrome(const char *s) {
    int len = (int)strlen(s);
    for (int i = 0; i < len / 2; i++)
        if (s[i] != s[len - 1 - i]) return false;
    return true;
}
